WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.880
Two GPS questions hide inside "does this reaction work?"

2
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.800
First: will this route actually reach the destination?

3
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.520
That's thermodynamics — ΔG and it tells you whether the reaction is favorable at

4
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.100
all. Second: how congested is the road?

5
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.020
That's kinetics — ΔG‡, double dagger, the activation energy and it tells you how

6
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.020
fast you'll get there.

7
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.320
Here's the line to remember: an enzyme answers only the second question.

8
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.960
It never changes whether a reaction can happen, only how fast.

9
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.653
Map the sign of delta ΔG onto a traffic light.

10
00:00:35.313 --> 00:00:38.713
Green — ΔG less than zero means go: the reaction is spontaneous.

11
00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:42.753
Yellow — ΔG equals zero is equilibrium, no net movement.

12
00:00:43.393 --> 00:00:47.853
Red — ΔG greater than zero means stop: the cell has to spend energy to push it

13
00:00:47.853 --> 00:00:52.433
forward. The crucial part is the caption: an enzyme cannot change the color of the

14
00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:55.953
light. It speeds the trip both ways toward the same equilibrium.

15
00:00:56.873 --> 00:00:59.773
Spontaneity belongs to thermodynamics, not the catalyst.

16
00:01:00.833 --> 00:01:02.493
A picture for the next section.

17
00:01:03.073 --> 00:01:07.673
Without an enzyme, reactants have to climb over a high mountain the long way around.

18
00:01:08.353 --> 00:01:11.193
With an enzyme, they take a shortcut through a lower pass.

19
00:01:11.973 --> 00:01:16.253
Notice both routes end at the same place on the far side: the enzyme doesn't move

20
00:01:16.253 --> 00:01:18.973
the destination, it just makes the crossing easier.

21
00:01:19.593 --> 00:01:21.573
So how exactly does it lower the pass?

22
00:01:21.573 --> 00:01:24.413
That's the transition-state secret, coming up.

23
00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:28.257
This is the single most important diagram in the chapter.

24
00:01:28.977 --> 00:01:33.657
Both curves start at the same substrate and end at the same product, so delta ΔG the

25
00:01:33.657 --> 00:01:37.217
overall free-energy change is identical with or without the enzyme.

26
00:01:37.917 --> 00:01:42.457
What changes is the height of the hill in between: the activation energy, delta ΔG‡,

27
00:01:42.457 --> 00:01:45.437
double dagger, is far lower when the enzyme is present.

28
00:01:46.317 --> 00:01:50.457
Enzymes speed reactions by stabilizing the transition state at the top of that hill,

29
00:01:50.837 --> 00:01:52.897
not by changing where the reaction ends up.

30
00:01:53.817 --> 00:01:57.697
The transition state is neither substrate nor product it's a fleeting,

31
00:01:57.877 --> 00:02:01.297
highest-energy arrangement of atoms that lasts only femtoseconds.

32
00:02:01.697 --> 00:02:06.357
The top row shows the arc: substrate in, transition state, product out.

33
00:02:06.897 --> 00:02:11.437
The bottom row zooms in on the chemistry bonds half-broken and half-formed at the

34
00:02:11.437 --> 00:02:17.157
same instant. The key insight: that transition state has a specific geometry, and

35
00:02:17.157 --> 00:02:20.617
it's the shape evolution has tuned the enzyme to recognize and grip.

36
00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.547
Four panels, one idea.

37
00:02:24.447 --> 00:02:28.727
First, the enzyme lowers the activation barrier by releasing binding energy right at

38
00:02:28.727 --> 00:02:29.727
the transition state.

39
00:02:30.327 --> 00:02:34.847
Second, shape complementarity: the active site fits the transition state better than

40
00:02:34.847 --> 00:02:36.247
it fits the ground-state substrate.

41
00:02:36.967 --> 00:02:40.867
Third, the barrier falls by the extra grip on the transition state, over the

42
00:02:40.867 --> 00:02:46.167
substrate. Fourth, the payoff in medicine: drugs shaped like the transition state

43
00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:49.867
exploit that tight fit, binding far harder than substrate mimics.

44
00:02:50.477 --> 00:02:55.407
The enzyme's job, in one line: bind the transition state tighter than the substrate.
